      'Setup example: 9 card(s) per player.',
      "Rule example: Each partnership aims to win at least five of the nine tricks. The team that wins the majority scores on a chalk-up by erasing strokes; the first side to erase all three strokes (or eliminate the opponents' crosses) scores a cross. Making vol (winning the first five tricks) or taking all nine tricks scores extra.",
      "Turn-flow example: The player to the left of the dealer leads to the first trick. Play is clockwise. Any card may be played; there is no requirement to follow suit or to beat the lead. Trick winner is determined by the game's ranking: permanent stikkar and chosen-suit stikkar beat other cards; chosen sevens (lambs) win the trick when led but cannot lead to the first trick. Whoever wins a trick leads to the next. A team that has taken five tricks may stop or continue; taking the first five (vol) or all nine scores bonus strokes.",
      'Scoring example: Chalk Marks. Vertical line with 3 cross strokes. Erase strokes as you win games. First to erase 3 strokes wins. Win 5 tricks out of 9..',
